  "passage": "At the beginning of the year, each student received a new notebook for writing practice. Most students filled the first page carefully.\nJack did not. He stared at the empty page for a long time because he was afraid of making mistakes.\nHis teacher noticed and wrote one sentence at the top: \"This notebook is for practice, not perfection.\"\nJack smiled and began writing.\nBy the end of the semester, his notebook had messy pages, crossed-out words, drawings, and many corrections. It was not beautiful, but it showed progress.\nJack learned that an empty page may look clean, but it cannot teach much. A used page, even a messy one, can show that learning happened.",
